{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SRigidityPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SRigidityPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SRigidity.S_bar_odd_of_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SRigidity.S_bar_odd_of_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SRigidityPrune.lean#L59-L71","doc":"**`S = Q_β/E₀` is bar-odd.** With `Q_β` bar-odd (`σ Q_β = −Q_β`, the sinh /\nCAL-2 = P_skew^β partner) and `E₀` bar-even (`σ E₀ = E₀`, the cosh / CAL-3 unit),\ntheir product form `Q_β · E₀⁻¹`… — stated multiplicatively as `S · E₀ = Q_β`\nto avoid an inverse, the honest content is: `σ (Q_β) = −Q_β` forces `S` bar-odd.\nHere we record the clean product version: if `S` satisfies `σ S = ε·S` and\n`σ E₀ = E₀` with `S·E₀ = Q_β` and `σ Q_β = −Q_β`, then the odd sign propagates.\nThe lemma states the carrier-parity step directly: a bar-odd numerator over a\nbar-fixed denominator-witness is bar-odd. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SRigidity.no_anchor_invariant_realizes_swing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SRigidity.no_anchor_invariant_realizes_swing","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SRigidityPrune.lean#L44-L57","doc":"**Anchor-invariant input cannot reproduce an anchor-varying target.**\nIf a candidate `g : D → R` is fed a datum `datum : A → D` that is *constant*\nacross two anchors (`datum a = datum a'`), then `g ∘ datum` is constant across\nthose anchors; so a target `S : A → R` with `S a ≠ S a'` is **not** realized by\n`g ∘ datum` at every anchor. Applied to `S = Q_β/E₀` (which swings: proton vs\nmuon) and any fixed CAL datum `𝔇` (`P_skew^β`, `P_avg^π`, `m_π`, all anchor-invariant):\n`S` is not a pure function of a single anchor-invariant calibration datum. ","signatureChunk":0}]}